
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TRACE-Omics in your research, please cite this software."
type: software

title: "TRACE-Omics: A Framework for Robust and Generalisable Transcriptomic Machine Learning"

authors:
  - family-names: Ehlers
    given-names: Ashley

abstract: >-
  TRACE-Omics is a research framework developed to investigate
  the robustness, reproducibility and cross-cohort generalisability
  of machine-learning models trained on high-dimensional
  transcriptomic data. The framework examines the influence
  of analytical pipeline choices, cohort heterogeneity and
  validation strategies on predictive performance.

keywords:
  - transcriptomics
  - machine learning
  - bioinformatics
  - computational biology
  - reproducibility
  - generalisability
  - cross-cohort validation
  - model transportability

repository-code: "https://github.com/AshleyPy/trace-omics"
url: "https://github.com/AshleyPy/trace-omics"

license: MIT

